# prometheus-postfix-exporter configuration
# This package configures the command-line arguments for the prometheus-postfix-exporter server.
#
# Schema Field: args
# Default: '' (empty string)
# Description: Command-line arguments to pass to the prometheus-postfix-exporter server.
#
# Note on escaping:
# - When running under systemd, shell escaping applies.
# - To pass a single backslash to the application via systemd, you typically need
#   to double it (e.g., '\\d' in the config becomes '\d' in the shell).
# - If the application itself requires a literal backslash, and systemd is involved,
#   you may need to quadruple it (\\\\d) depending on how the systemd ExecStart
#   directive processes the string. Consult the specific exporter documentation.

# Set the command-line arguments to pass to the prometheus-postfix-exporter server.
# If left empty, the server will run with default arguments.
ARGS="{{ args | default('') }}"